# VTID-03938 — commands run during this change

## Investigation (via Explore subagent, then independently verified)
Found the bug: fetchExistingPendingInvitation() checks only
accepted_at/revoked_at, never expires_at. Confirmed directly by reading
services/gateway/src/services/tenant-invitations/tenant-invitations-repository.ts
lines 23-32 and services/gateway/test/routes/tenant-admin/invitations.test.ts
(no existing test covers the expired-and-unrevoked scenario).

## Fix
Added `.gt('expires_at', new Date().toISOString())` to the query in
fetchExistingPendingInvitation().

## Test infrastructure fix (required, not optional)
The mock chain in invitations.test.ts's createChain() had no `.gt()`
method — added `gt: jest.fn(() => chain)` alongside the existing
eq/gte/is/not mocks. Without this, every test hitting POST / would throw
TypeError: chain.gt is not a function once the real code called it.

## New regression test
Added "POST / allows re-inviting once the previous invitation has expired
(VTID-03938)" — asserts both the 201 outcome and that chain.gt was called
with ('expires_at', <ISO string>), since the outcome alone can't
distinguish "filtered correctly" from "filter never added" under this
mock's architecture (it resolves purely from queued values).

